window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ayanokouji-atsuomi"]=[{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka matsuo chabashira-sae ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 3  the drop out demand sits opposite the sweating principal in the office  delivers the prepared drop out papers and the matsuo leverage   how about you take a seat  i came all the way here to meet with you  after all   friends  don t make me laugh  there s no way you re capable of making friends   then i assume you re going to do as i say  no need to discuss anything  i m busy anyway   i ve prepared the documents necessary for you to drop out  i spoke to the principal about it  all i need is for you to say yes   for you  that might be true  but i have my own reasons   parent  you ve never recognized me as your parent before   the fact is that you ve been behaving selfishly  i ordered you to remain on standby   you re my property  a man may do as he wishes with his property  whether i keep you alive or kill you is up to me   don t you wonder how matsuo s doing  the person who told you about this school and gave you the idea to enroll   i hired him to manage you for a year in his capacity as a butler  but he chose to go against his employer   an outrageous  unforgiveable act  naturally  matsuo had to be punished   you can probably guess what i m about to say   but now he s been expelled   matsuo s son was strong  even though he was expelled from the school on which he d pinned his hopes  his determination didn t fade  he   bounced back and immediately tried to enroll in other schools  i did whatever was necessary to crush his attempts to advance  i made him give up  i did the same to matsuo  too  i tarnished his reputation  leaving him unable to find a job  his son also lost his way  and is now unemployed   he begged me to leave the boy alone  and committed suicide last month by self immolation   right now  his son s working part time  earning enough to live on and nothing else  with no guarantee of a future  no dreams  no hope  his family s tragedy is your fault  the boy must surely bear a deep grudge against you  even in death  he won t forgive you   the man who took care of you  who saved you  has died  and you show no reaction whatsoever  if matsuo could see you now  he d be full of regret   matsuo s death has already been recorded  if necessary  i can send for the papers confirming it   you ve changed quite a bit  kiyotaka   what happened that year  what made you so determined to go to this school   i don t entirely understand  but it seems that i have no choice but to accept  i suppose that temporarily suspending the facility s activity was a mistake  to think that a plan sixteen years in the making could be ruined in just a year   i understand why you re here   but if you think the matter is settled  you re naive  as with matsuo s son  i can force you to quit   that s a statement made without proof   there s no need to bring a bodyguard along to visit a high school   did matsuo put that idea in your head  even in death  he s still impeding me   why would someone like you veer off your path  you were taught from the very beginning that there was no point learning unnecessary things   utter nonsense  the only path in this world is the one i prepared for you  you will one day surpass me  and become the person who guides japan into the future  why can t you understand that   it seems i can t get through to you   the white room has resumed operations  this time  my plans are perfect  nothing will get in the way  i m prepared to make up for lost time  son across the table  the whole scene is their first face to face in a year and a half  dead butler used as leverage  self immolation last month after the son s prospects were crushed  bows out with the principal  her nerves framed the visit  ruined a butler s reputation  a son s schooling and a family s future without raising his voice  treats the suicide as a report  views his son as property  speaks in corporate and white room absolutes  admits the sixteen year plan broke in one year  still claims the single prepared path  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the drop-out demand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.55–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits opposite the sweating principal in the office; delivers the prepared drop-out papers and the Matsuo leverage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"matsuo.html\">Matsuo<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about you take a seat? I came all the way here to meet with you, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Friends? Don’t make me laugh. There’s no way you’re capable of making friends,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Then I assume you’re going to do as I say. No need to discuss anything; I’m busy anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve prepared the documents necessary for you to drop out. I spoke to the principal about it. All I need is for you to say yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For you, that might be true. But I have my own reasons.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Parent? You’ve never recognized me as your parent before,”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The fact is that you’ve been behaving selfishly. I ordered you to remain on standby,”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re my property. A man may do as he wishes with his property. Whether I keep you alive or kill you is up to me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you wonder how Matsuo’s doing? The person who told you about this school and gave you the idea to enroll?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hired him to manage you for a year in his capacity as a butler, but he chose to go against his employer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An outrageous, unforgiveable act. Naturally, Matsuo had to be punished.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can probably guess what I’m about to say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now he’s been expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Matsuo’s son was strong. Even though he was expelled from the school on which he’d pinned his hopes, his determination didn’t fade. He … bounced back and immediately tried to enroll in other schools. I did whatever was necessary to crush his attempts to advance. I made him give up. I did the same to Matsuo, too. I tarnished his reputation, leaving him unable to find a job. His son also lost his way, and is now unemployed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He begged me to leave the boy alone, and committed suicide last month by self-immolation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now, his son’s working part-time, earning enough to live on and nothing else, with no guarantee of a future. No dreams. No hope. His family’s tragedy is your fault. The boy must surely bear a deep grudge against you. Even in death, he won’t forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The man who took care of you, who saved you, has died. And you show no reaction whatsoever. If Matsuo could see you now, he’d be full of regret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Matsuo’s death has already been recorded. If necessary, I can send for the papers confirming it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve changed quite a bit, Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happened that year? What made you so determined to go to this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t entirely understand, but it seems that I have no choice but to accept. I suppose that temporarily suspending the facility’s activity was a mistake. To think that a plan sixteen years in the making could be ruined in just a year…”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand why you’re here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if you think the matter is settled, you’re naïve. As with Matsuo’s son, I can force you to quit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a statement made without proof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to bring a bodyguard along to visit a high school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did Matsuo put that idea in your head? Even in death, he’s still impeding me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why would someone like you veer off your path? You were taught from the very beginning that there was no point learning unnecessary things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Utter nonsense. The only path in this world is the one I prepared for you. You will one day surpass me, and become the person who guides Japan into the future. Why can’t you understand that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems I can’t get through to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The White Room has resumed operations. This time, my plans are perfect. Nothing will get in the way. I’m prepared to make up for lost time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Son across the table; the whole scene is their first face-to-face in a year and a half.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsuo<\/b> Dead butler used as leverage; self-immolation last month after the son’s prospects were crushed.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Bows out with the principal; her nerves framed the visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ruined a butler’s reputation, a son’s schooling and a family’s future without raising his voice; treats the suicide as a report.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Views his son as property; speaks in corporate and White Room absolutes; admits the sixteen-year plan broke in one year; still claims the single prepared path.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the ultimatum answered<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 3  the ultimatum answered gets the free will refusal  watches sakayanagi block the expulsion on autonomy and tuition rules  and leaves without a card left   am i to assume a parent can t lie to their own child   you have no plans to return   how foolish  this school s nothing more than a barn full of common rabble  i m sure that your own class holds many such worthless bottomfeeders with no hope of salvation   you think that even incompetent morons can stand toe to toe with geniuses   you want to destroy my ideals  then   we should end this  we know that  no matter how long we talk  we ll never agree   that s right  since it s what his parent wishes  the school must immediately take appropriate action   you ve changed  too  where did the old  agreeable you go   you re free to succeed your father and carry on his wishes  however  if that s your intention  then why did you allow kiyotaka to enter this school   don t dodge the question  this school s fundamentally unlike ordinary schools  kiyotaka should never have been a suitable candidate for admission  i know that the interviews and exam are just for show   kiyotaka never should ve been among the possible candidates in the first place  it s abnormal that you didn t disqualify him   don t screw with me   if that s how things stand  i ll find another way   i understand  i haven t the slightest intention of putting any pressure on you   in that case  we re done talking  if you ll please excuse me   when will we meet again   coming to a place like this once is quite enough  free will answer  parting jab about visiting the school again ignored  chairman sakayanagi  father  blocks him on autonomy and government fees  nostalgia for the old agreeable days  falls back to  find another way  and rule compliant expulsion once the three way talk offer lands  ideologue about genius and rabble  admits no pressure while implying force  leaves rather than argue with the board","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the ultimatum answered<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.65–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gets the free-will refusal, watches Sakayanagi block the expulsion on autonomy and tuition rules, and leaves without a card left.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Am I to assume a parent can’t lie to their own child?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have no plans to return?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How foolish. This school’s nothing more than a barn full of common rabble. I’m sure that your own class holds many such worthless bottomfeeders with no hope of salvation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You think that even incompetent morons can stand toe-to-toe with geniuses?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to destroy my ideals, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We should end this. We know that, no matter how long we talk, we’ll never agree.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. Since it’s what his parent wishes, the school must immediately take appropriate action.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve changed, too. Where did the old, agreeable you go?”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to succeed your father and carry on his wishes. However, if that’s your intention, then why did you allow Kiyotaka to enter this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t dodge the question. This school’s fundamentally unlike ordinary schools. Kiyotaka should never have been a suitable candidate for admission. I know that the interviews and exam are just for show,”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kiyotaka never should’ve been among the possible candidates in the first place. It’s abnormal that you didn’t disqualify him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t screw with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s how things stand, I’ll find another way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. I haven’t the slightest intention of putting any pressure on you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, we’re done talking. If you’ll please excuse me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When will we meet again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Coming to a place like this once is quite enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Free-will answer; parting jab about visiting the school again ignored.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Chairman Sakayanagi (father) blocks him on autonomy and government fees; nostalgia for the old agreeable days.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Falls back to “find another way” and rule-compliant expulsion once the three-way-talk offer lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ideologue about genius and rabble; admits no pressure while implying force; leaves rather than argue with the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y1v7-p55-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the drop-out demand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v3-p49-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ayanokoji  father  mentioned in passing named in the context of the white room  named in the context of the exam  passing mentions  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v3-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ayanokōji (father) mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.49–50, 125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the context of the White Room. Named in the context of the exam.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–50, 125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–50, 125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4_5-p10-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ayanokouji atsuomi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 17 18  p 20  p 22  p 25 26  p 29 30  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">ayanokouji-atsuomi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10-290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.17-18, p.20, p.22, p.25-26, p.29-30.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7-243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v6-p11-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v6-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.11-346<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v7-p7-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v7-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7-207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_75-p4-1","v":"y2v9.75","y":2,"o":27,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v9_75-p4-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.75 · p.4-8<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10_25-p1-1","v":"y2v10.25","y":2,"o":29,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v10_25-p1-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10.25 · p.1-10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11-223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v12_5-p107-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi ch 7 mentioned appears in ch 7  appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y2v12_5-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.107-121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned/appears in Ch.7.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Appears in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.107-121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi a life carved out of disparity and ambition atsuomi reflects on his origins in his own monologue   born poor  uneducated and in the countryside  with nothing but youth and an  indefinitely expanding ambition   rich  poor the disparity of wealth   this japan is a society of disparities   while i understood that principle  i possessed nothing   i was born in the countryside  extremely poor  and so uneducated it was pitiful   it was an indefinitely expanding  ambition one that couldn t be suppressed   i will definitely rise and stand at the pinnacle of this country  defines himself by disparity and a single  suppressless ambition to reach the pinnacle of the country   the only support he had in life  frames the whole volume as his monologue looking back on the path that led to the white room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">A life carved out of disparity and ambition<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.10–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Atsuomi reflects on his origins in his own monologue — born poor, uneducated and in the countryside, with nothing but youth and an &quot;indefinitely expanding ambition.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;RICH, POOR—THE DISPARITY of wealth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;This Japan is a society of disparities.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;While I understood that principle, I possessed nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I was born in the countryside, extremely poor, and so uneducated it was pitiful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It was an indefinitely expanding &#x27;ambition&#x27;—one that couldn&#x27;t be suppressed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I will definitely rise and stand at the pinnacle of this country.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Defines himself by disparity and a single, suppressless ambition to reach the pinnacle of the country — the only support he had in life.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Frames the whole volume as his monologue looking back on the path that led to the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\">→ After: The failed election and the backroom rise<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the failed election and the backroom rise  at twenty five  i gained my first right to be elected   it was a fleeting  foolish dream  i underestimated the election and was miserably defeated   what was important in winning an election was which organization you belonged to and whom you followed   i requested to join the ruling  citizens  party  and began my steps as a politician   i took on the dirty backroom jobs that nobody wanted to do   eventually  as a secret blade for  naoe sensei  who controlled many factions within the citizens  party  i unhesitatingly delved into any wrongdoing facilitating underage girls  giving bribes  and committing espionage against rival organizations   at the age of thirty six  i had one foot in the realm of power  pragmatic and utterly unscrupulous   learns that power  not ideals  wins elections and becomes naoe sensei s  secret blade  committing any wrongdoing for advancement  becomes his secret blade  regards him as a stepping stone to be eventually surpassed and crushed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The failed election and the backroom rise<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.11–12<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;At twenty-five, I gained my first right to be elected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It was a fleeting, foolish dream. I underestimated the election and was miserably defeated.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;What was important in winning an election was which organization you belonged to and whom you followed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I requested to join the ruling &#x27;Citizens&#x27; Party&#x27; and began my steps as a politician.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I took on the dirty backroom jobs that nobody wanted to do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Eventually, as a secret blade for &#x27;Naoe-sensei,&#x27; who controlled many factions within the Citizens&#x27; Party, I unhesitatingly delved into any wrongdoing—facilitating underage girls, giving bribes, and committing espionage against rival organizations.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;At the age of thirty-six, I had one foot in the realm of power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pragmatic and utterly unscrupulous — learns that power, not ideals, wins elections and becomes Naoe-sensei&#x27;s &quot;secret blade,&quot; committing any wrongdoing for advancement.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Becomes his secret blade; regards him as a stepping stone to be eventually surpassed and crushed.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p10-1\">← Before: A life carved out of disparity and ambition<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\">→ After: The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"tabuchi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the newborn and the white room s fourth phase his child is born  he views the newborn with no emotion beyond relief at the political lever it represents   a newborn arrived  just one month old   no special emotions arose not a single one   if anything  i was relieved that the key to moving the higher ups had arrived   there are currently no issues  there were no problems found in various tests  including the brain waves    tabuchi s report  like the previous children  start the experiment immediately  coldly instrumental   sees his own son as a  key to moving the higher ups  feels nothing  and orders the experiment to begin at once  tabuchi runs the health dna tests and reports the results  atsuomi orders him to start the experiment  his newborn son  immediately entered into the white room experiment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.12–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His child is born; he views the newborn with no emotion beyond relief at the political lever it represents.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#tabuchi\">Tabuchi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;A newborn arrived, just one month old.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;No special emotions arose—not a single one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;If anything, I was relieved that the key to moving the higher-ups had arrived.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;There are currently no issues. There were no problems found in various tests, including the brain waves.&quot; — Tabuchi&#x27;s report<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Like the previous children, start the experiment immediately.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly instrumental — sees his own son as a &quot;key to moving the higher-ups,&quot; feels nothing, and orders the experiment to begin at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tabuchi<\/b> Tabuchi runs the health/DNA tests and reports the results; Atsuomi orders him to start the experiment.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His newborn son, immediately entered into the White Room experiment.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p11-1\">← Before: The failed election and the backroom rise<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\">→ After: The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi tabuchi naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top holds his son through the glass before the white room  staging an emotional farewell for the cameras   this child is more important than my own life  and i m sending him to the white room  capture the determination and tension on camera   a parent who s indifferent about leaving their child  and a parent who reluctantly entrusts their child for the future   anyway  all the necessary preparations are now complete  connect me to sakayanagi   i would use anything  even my own child  discard it  and reach the top   even someone with absolute authority  like naoe sensei  was no different as a stepping stone   if you don t want to die  you better struggle on your own  kiyotaka   the turning point came about four years after i started working under naoe sensei  calculated and ruthless   stages a reluctant father image for fundraising  treats his child and naoe sensei alike as disposable stepping stones  and addresses kiyotaka with a parting challenge to survive alone  sends him to the white room as the fourth phase subject  tells him he must struggle on his own  requests to be connected to him once preparations are complete  directs him to capture the staged farewell on camera  resolves to eventually surpass and crush him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.15–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds his son through the glass before the White Room, staging an emotional farewell for the cameras.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#tabuchi\">Tabuchi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;This child is more important than my own life, and I&#x27;m sending him to the White Room. Capture the determination and tension on camera.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;A parent who&#x27;s indifferent about leaving their child, and a parent who reluctantly entrusts their child for the future.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Anyway, all the necessary preparations are now complete. Connect me to Sakayanagi.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I would use anything, even my own child, discard it, and reach the top.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Even someone with absolute authority, like Naoe-sensei, was no different as a stepping stone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;If you don&#x27;t want to die, you better struggle on your own, Kiyotaka.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;The turning point came about four years after I started working under Naoe-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculated and ruthless — stages a reluctant-father image for fundraising, treats his child and Naoe-sensei alike as disposable stepping stones, and addresses Kiyotaka with a parting challenge to survive alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sends him to the White Room as the fourth-phase subject; tells him he must struggle on his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sakayanagi<\/b> Requests to be connected to him once preparations are complete.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tabuchi<\/b> Directs him to capture the staged farewell on camera.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Resolves to eventually surpass and crush him.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p12-1\">← Before: The newborn and the White Room&#x27;s fourth phase<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\">→ After: Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi waiting for naoe sensei  on kamogawa waits an hour in the freezing cold outside ryoutei sasagawa for naoe sensei  with kamogawa   it s always like this  for naoe sensei  the appointed time is merely a guideline   you re naive  we re lucky if he comes here today at all  oftentimes  he doesn t even show up   even being late is a weapon for naoe sensei  like the anecdote of miyamoto musashi at ganryujima   it would be troublesome if you look down on naoe sensei i ll just dismiss them like that   they say that seeking hardship is good  even if you have to pay for it  but i ve been hit once or twice  patient  loyal and world weary   treats naoe s lateness as deliberate power  absorbs the anger of those kept waiting  and despises the spoiled second generation politicians  manages and lectures the complaining rookie  sees him as a leech who wants only to survive  serves as his intermediary and shielding face  absorbing resentment so naoe never has to","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.17–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits an hour in the freezing cold outside Ryoutei Sasagawa for Naoe-sensei, with Kamogawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s always like this. For Naoe-sensei, the appointed time is merely a guideline.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;You&#x27;re naive. We&#x27;re lucky if he comes here today at all. Oftentimes, he doesn&#x27;t even show up.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Even being late is a weapon for Naoe-sensei. Like the anecdote of Miyamoto Musashi at Ganryujima.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;It would be troublesome if you look down on Naoe-sensei—I&#x27;ll just dismiss them like that.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;They say that seeking hardship is good, even if you have to pay for it, but I&#x27;ve been hit once or twice.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Patient, loyal and world-weary — treats Naoe&#x27;s lateness as deliberate power, absorbs the anger of those kept waiting, and despises the spoiled second-generation politicians.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Manages and lectures the complaining rookie; sees him as a leech who wants only to survive.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Serves as his intermediary and shielding face, absorbing resentment so Naoe never has to.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p15-1\">← Before: The staged goodbye and the vow to reach the top<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\">→ After: Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"asama kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi naoe arrives  the meeting with asama naoe s taxi arrives  atsuomi stops kamogawa from reacting rashly when a woman is seen with him   don t do anything rash   good work today  naoe sensei   where is asama   he s been waiting  i ll guide you   asama sensei  i ve brought naoe sensei  refuses the temptation to eavesdrop on the two major politicians   scheming would be exposed and end his career  vigilant and disciplined   shields naoe from embarrassment  reads the room  and withdraws rather than risk the  devil s  temptation to gather information  guides naoe to the waiting asama hisashi  notes the instant master servant role reversal  signals him to pay the fare and keeps him in line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.20–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naoe&#x27;s taxi arrives; Atsuomi stops Kamogawa from reacting rashly when a woman is seen with him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#asama\">Asama<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Don&#x27;t do anything rash.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Good work today, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Where is Asama?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;He&#x27;s been waiting. I&#x27;ll guide you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Asama-sensei, I&#x27;ve brought Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Refuses the temptation to eavesdrop on the two major politicians — scheming would be exposed and end his career.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Vigilant and disciplined — shields Naoe from embarrassment, reads the room, and withdraws rather than risk the &quot;devil&#x27;s&quot; temptation to gather information.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asama<\/b> Guides Naoe to the waiting Asama Hisashi; notes the instant master-servant role reversal.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Signals him to pay the fare and keeps him in line.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p17-1\">← Before: Waiting for Naoe-sensei; on Kamogawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\">→ After: The private room: seiza and the sake<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the private room  seiza and the sake in a separate private room with kamogawa  warns him not to drink the ceremonial sake   don t drink the sake   are you planning to send off naoe sensei with the smell of alcohol  this is nothing more than a formality   it s a habit  in front of naoe sensei and the others  i have to sit in seiza for hours without any trouble  abstains from sake after witnessing a predecessor erased for it  and keeps himself in seiza always so formal occasions cost him nothing  teaches him the room s unspoken rules","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The private room: seiza and the sake<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.24–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In a separate private room with Kamogawa, warns him not to drink the ceremonial sake.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Don&#x27;t drink the sake.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Are you planning to send off Naoe-sensei with the smell of alcohol? This is nothing more than a formality.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s a habit. In front of Naoe-sensei and the others, I have to sit in seiza for hours without any trouble.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Abstains from sake after witnessing a predecessor erased for it, and keeps himself in seiza always so formal occasions cost him nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Teaches him the room&#x27;s unspoken rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p20-1\">← Before: Naoe arrives; the meeting with Asama<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\">→ After: Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kijima isomaru ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi naoe s summons  kijima and the project envelope summoned by naoe after the meeting to another private room  with kijima s untouched cups evident   this is my fourth year studying under you  sensei   i m truly thankful  naoe sensei  you picked up someone like me   i believe he has many achievements  but if there s something to highlight  it would be  anhs   you must be joking  whether it s the present or future  the only person i will learn from is you  naoe sensei  carefully deferential   deflects naoe s praise  declares loyalty  and correctly identifies kijima s anhs as his rise  views him as the  have not  who rose fastest  naoe probes his loyalty and hints at a new project  identified by naoe as the greatest enemy  a young  clean  spotlight politician rising on anhs  naoe s rival  the third ranking party figure   old fashioned and straightforward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.27–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned by Naoe after the meeting to another private room, with Kijima&#x27;s untouched cups evident.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kijima.html\">Kijima<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#isomaru\">Isomaru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;This is my fourth year studying under you, Sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m truly thankful, Naoe-sensei. You picked up someone like me.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I believe he has many achievements, but if there&#x27;s something to highlight, it would be &#x27;ANHS&#x27;.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;You must be joking. Whether it&#x27;s the present or future, the only person I will learn from is you, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully deferential — deflects Naoe&#x27;s praise, declares loyalty, and correctly identifies Kijima&#x27;s ANHS as his rise.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Views him as the &quot;have-not&quot; who rose fastest; Naoe probes his loyalty and hints at a new project.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kijima<\/b> Identified by Naoe as the greatest enemy; a young, clean, spotlight politician rising on ANHS.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Isomaru<\/b> Naoe&#x27;s rival, the third-ranking party figure — old-fashioned and straightforward.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p24-1\">← Before: The private room: seiza and the sake<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\">→ After: &quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi  what makes a politician outstanding  naoe poses a drinking game question to kamogawa and atsuomi   although i m inexperienced  i think of someone like you  naoe sensei   a bad politician serves tempura to a customer who wants sushi   a customer is a customer  sometimes they are the citizens  sometimes they are politicians  and sometimes they are something else altogether   a good politician serves delicious sushi to a customer who wants sushi  probably  only about thirty percent  no  maybe only twenty percent of politicians can do this   if you re going to call a politician  exceptionally outstanding  more is required  even if a customer wants sushi  they can guide them to be fully satisfied with curry or beef bowl   when i had just started studying under you  naoe sensei  you once told me that people s actions are determined by their goals   i will devote my whole heart and soul to this task  articulate and ambitious   defines a truly outstanding politician as one who can redirect desire to a satisfying alternative  then accepts naoe s envelope project with a bow  knowing failure would ash his four years  challenges and delights him with the sushi metaphor  accepts the envelope project that promises fame  watches him give a simplistic answer about responding to the citizens  wishes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">&quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.31–33<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naoe poses a drinking-game question to Kamogawa and Atsuomi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Although I&#x27;m inexperienced, I think of someone like you, Naoe-sensei.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;A bad politician serves tempura to a customer who wants sushi.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;A customer is a customer. Sometimes they are the citizens, sometimes they are politicians, and sometimes they are something else altogether.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;A good politician serves delicious sushi to a customer who wants sushi. Probably, only about thirty percent... no, maybe only twenty percent of politicians can do this.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;If you&#x27;re going to call a politician &#x27;exceptionally outstanding,&#x27; more is required. Even if a customer wants sushi, they can guide them to be fully satisfied with curry or beef bowl.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;When I had just started studying under you, Naoe-sensei, you once told me that people&#x27;s actions are determined by their goals.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I will devote my whole heart and soul to this task.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Articulate and ambitious — defines a truly outstanding politician as one who can redirect desire to a satisfying alternative, then accepts Naoe&#x27;s envelope project with a bow, knowing failure would ash his four years.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Challenges and delights him with the sushi metaphor; accepts the envelope project that promises fame.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Watches him give a simplistic answer about responding to the citizens&#x27; wishes.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p27-1\">← Before: Naoe&#x27;s summons: Kijima and the project envelope<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\">→ After: Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ooba naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi planning the human resource development project  using kamogawa at his cluttered office  plans the  human resource development project    gathering newborns and securing a huge budget   this project is going to be troublesome   it s me  put ooba on  i have a new job for him   kamogawa  i m telling you this for your own good  don t mimic the likes of kisarazu   i m not saying don t buy real estate  i m just saying don t miss the right timing  money is finite  but it holds infinite possibilities   can you be of use   for the project in question  it s essential to secure an experimental facility  i ll leave the location selection to you   from a budgetary perspective  seems like it ll inevitably be in the countryside   there are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into  ruthlessly pragmatic   uses whatever pieces work regardless of morality  contacts the criminal ooba group to acquire newborns  and manipulates kamogawa with small praise into useful service  puts him to work selecting a facility location and securing funding  knows a little praise makes him useful  contacts him about acquiring newborns   evil means are unavoidable  notes naoe could make funds appear with one word  since he can t  a major investor is urgently needed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.42–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At his cluttered office, plans the &quot;Human Resource Development Project&quot; — gathering newborns and securing a huge budget.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ooba\">Ooba<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;…This project is going to be troublesome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;It&#x27;s me. Put Ooba on. I have a new job for him.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Kamogawa. I&#x27;m telling you this for your own good, don&#x27;t mimic the likes of Kisarazu.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m not saying don&#x27;t buy real estate. I&#x27;m just saying don&#x27;t miss the right timing. Money is finite, but it holds infinite possibilities.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Can you be of use?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;For the project in question, it&#x27;s essential to secure an experimental facility. I&#x27;ll leave the location selection to you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;From a budgetary perspective, seems like it&#x27;ll inevitably be in the countryside.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;There are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthlessly pragmatic — uses whatever pieces work regardless of morality, contacts the criminal Ooba group to acquire newborns, and manipulates Kamogawa with small praise into useful service.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Puts him to work selecting a facility location and securing funding; knows a little praise makes him useful.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ooba<\/b> Contacts him about acquiring newborns — evil means are unavoidable.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Notes Naoe could make funds appear with one word; since he can&#x27;t, a major investor is urgently needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p31-1\">← Before: &quot;What makes a politician outstanding&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\">→ After: Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi visiting sakayanagi narimori for funding visits the sakayanagi mansion in shirokane to ask for help funding the project   nice to meet you  my name is ayanokouji  thank you for making time in your busy schedule   i recalled naoe sensei saying that if i ever had a problem  i could rely on you  sakayanagi san that s why i ve come to visit  sakayanagi narimori  arisu s father  receives him   slender  gentle  feigning humility  he says naoe spoke highly of ayanokouji and that they are the same age  his own lines are recorded on his own card  confident but mannerly   chooses to sit without making himself small  while knowing he is the one asking a favor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.48–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Visits the Sakayanagi mansion in Shirokane to ask for help funding the project.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Nice to meet you. My name is Ayanokouji. Thank you for making time in your busy schedule.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I recalled Naoe-sensei saying that if I ever had a problem, I could rely on you, Sakayanagi-san—that&#x27;s why I&#x27;ve come to visit.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi Narimori (Arisu&#x27;s father) receives him — slender, gentle, feigning humility. He says Naoe spoke highly of Ayanokouji and that they are the same age. His own lines are recorded on his own card.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Confident but mannerly — chooses to sit without making himself small, while knowing he is the one asking a favor.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p42-1\">← Before: Planning the Human Resource Development Project; using Kamogawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\">→ After: The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the white room facility named  the mentor s warning reviews photos of the finished facility in saitama  kamogawa reports construction complete   we ll call it white room  we want to emphasize white s purity in the image   there are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into   kamogawa  i need to teach you something important  the world of politics isn t just about friends or foes   never mind  it seems it was too soon for you  sees the  white room  name as image strategy  knows he walks a bridge that could collapse and tries  in vain  to warn the naive kamogawa  credits him for moving the financial world  judges him not yet ready to understand political danger","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.70–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reviews photos of the finished facility in Saitama; Kamogawa reports construction complete.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;We&#x27;ll call it White Room. We want to emphasize white&#x27;s purity in the image.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;There are more than a few construction companies that would have its dirt revealed when dug into.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Kamogawa, I need to teach you something important. The world of politics isn&#x27;t just about friends or foes.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Never mind. It seems it was too soon for you.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees the &quot;White Room&quot; name as image strategy; knows he walks a bridge that could collapse and tries (in vain) to warn the naive Kamogawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Credits him for moving the financial world; judges him not yet ready to understand political danger.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p48-1\">← Before: Visiting Sakayanagi Narimori for funding<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\">→ After: Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"souya kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi hiring souya and the other  problem  experts interviews souya  a disgraced former doctor  for the research lab   i haven t told you that you re hired yet   i don t care about your career   which university you graduated from  which hospital you worked at  what crimes you ve committed i have no interest in any of that   i m only interested in your current thoughts and abilities   i ll give you a chance to resurrect yourself   he has no close associates around him  he s obsessed with money and doesn t seek honor from the outside world   we ll let the people we hire compete  then  the answers will naturally emerge  coldly exploitative   hires competent outcasts who can be paid and controlled  pits experts against each other to reveal ability  and fires without mercy if results disappoint  hires him on the spot as a researcher former doctor to manage the subjects  lets him observe  dismisses his worries about hiring such people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.72–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Interviews Souya, a disgraced former doctor, for the research lab.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#souya\">Sōya<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I haven&#x27;t told you that you&#x27;re hired yet.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;I don&#x27;t care about your career.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Which university you graduated from, which hospital you worked at, what crimes you&#x27;ve committed—I have no interest in any of that.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;m only interested in your current thoughts and abilities.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I&#x27;ll give you a chance to resurrect yourself.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;He has no close associates around him. He&#x27;s obsessed with money and doesn&#x27;t seek honor from the outside world.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;We&#x27;ll let the people we hire compete. Then, the answers will naturally emerge.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly exploitative — hires competent outcasts who can be paid and controlled, pits experts against each other to reveal ability, and fires without mercy if results disappoint.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sōya<\/b> Hires him on the spot as a researcher/former doctor to manage the subjects.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Lets him observe; dismisses his worries about hiring such people.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p70-1\">← Before: The White Room facility named; the mentor&#x27;s warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro: the journalist&#x27;s body and the background check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"tsukishiro naoe-sensei ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi tsukishiro  the journalist s body and the background check finds tsukishiro s business card on the floor after the interviews  arranges to meet him   then we ll get things started now  i won t let you say it s impossible   you bastard   that isn t it  huh  you re probably just keeping an eye on a politician to replace me   i don t care about that  what i want to know is whether you were impersonating naoe sensei when this journalist met you at the restaurant   at least i wouldn t be foolish enough to allow the body to be found   there are many things i dislike about this  but you can t make an omelet without breaking eggs    corpus reads  you can t make an omelet   i understand  how much   it was a dugout shed used to store agricultural tools managed by the neighborhood adults  realizes the journalist s body was intentionally left found   to chill the  rats  watching naoe  with an unknown scapegoat set to take the blame  unfazed by a possible killer   feels anger rather than fear  reads tsukishiro s strategy  and agrees to work with him while calmly disclosing his deprived childhood  meets him  recognizes him as naoe s observer cleanup man and supporter  and decides to use him to recruit personnel  realizes naoe had tsukishiro watching insuring the project from the start","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tsukishiro: the journalist&#x27;s body and the background check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.76–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Tsukishiro&#x27;s business card on the floor after the interviews; arranges to meet him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;Then we&#x27;ll get things started now. I won&#x27;t let you say it&#x27;s impossible.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;…You bastard.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;&#x27;That isn&#x27;t it, huh? You&#x27;re probably just keeping an eye on a politician to replace me.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I don&#x27;t care about that. What I want to know is whether you were impersonating Naoe-sensei when this journalist met you at the restaurant.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;At least I wouldn&#x27;t be foolish enough to allow the body to be found.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;There are many things I dislike about this, but you can&#x27;t make an omelet without breaking eggs.&#x27;&quot; — corpus reads &quot;you can&#x27;t make an omelet&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;I understand. How much?&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;&#x27;It was a dugout shed used to store agricultural tools managed by the neighborhood adults.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes the journalist&#x27;s body was intentionally left found — to chill the &quot;rats&quot; watching Naoe, with an unknown scapegoat set to take the blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unfazed by a possible killer — feels anger rather than fear, reads Tsukishiro&#x27;s strategy, and agrees to work with him while calmly disclosing his deprived childhood.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Meets him; recognizes him as Naoe&#x27;s observer/cleanup man and supporter, and decides to use him to recruit personnel.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> Realizes Naoe had Tsukishiro watching/insuring the project from the start.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p72-1\">← Before: Hiring Souya and the other &quot;problem&quot; experts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p96-1\">→ After: The drive to the facility; three years of the White Room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p96-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the drive to the facility  three years of the white room dozes in the back seat of a car on rough mountain roads  heading to the white room three years after the project began  the car has genuine leather seats  deep and soft   far more luxurious  than his old used kei car  his dream recalls the used kei car he bought as a teen   over a hundred thousand kilometers on it  interior barely maintained   a clunker  yet he felt like head of a household driving it  he made no friends or lovers then  time alone with the car was irreplaceable  the urban scenery gave way to rough roads surrounded by mountains  the driver warns it will be bumpy   three years had passed since naoe sensei entrusted me with the human resource development project  the project  officially named the white room project  began in secrecy  financiers grew daily and funds were in surplus  the white room became a status symbol known only to those in the know  illegitimate children placed by mistresses to erase them publicly exceeded 30  of the second batch of children  he views the children overwhelmingly as experimental subjects  not charges  keeps distance from the political world and wears  both the masks of a politician and a financier","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The drive to the facility; three years of the White Room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.96–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dozes in the back seat of a car on rough mountain roads, heading to the White Room three years after the project began.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Three years had passed since Naoe-sensei entrusted me with the Human Resource Development Project.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The car has genuine leather seats, deep and soft, &quot;far more luxurious&quot; than his old used kei car.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> His dream recalls the used kei car he bought as a teen — over a hundred thousand kilometers on it, interior barely maintained, &quot;a clunker,&quot; yet he felt like head of a household driving it.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He made no friends or lovers then; time alone with the car was irreplaceable.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The urban scenery gave way to rough roads surrounded by mountains; the driver warns it will be bumpy.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The project, officially named the White Room Project, began in secrecy; financiers grew daily and funds were in surplus; the White Room became a status symbol known only to those in the know.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Illegitimate children placed by mistresses to erase them publicly exceeded 30% of the second batch of children.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He views the children overwhelmingly as experimental subjects, not charges; keeps distance from the political world and wears &quot;both the masks of a politician and a financier.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96–100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p76-1\">← Before: Tsukishiro: the journalist&#x27;s body and the background check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p101-1\">→ After: Showing Sakayanagi the lab; the exam setup<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p101-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-narimori ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi showing sakayanagi the lab  the exam setup greets sakayanagi at the guest room   he had been standing looking out the window rather than sitting on the sofa   sorry to keep you waiting   it can t be helped  we can t make this public right now  there are countless people desperately searching for scandals involving me and naoe sensei   you were the one who helped with the white room project the most  i wanted to show it to you first   no  for these three years  i ve basically been hands off  i ve just continued to provide the necessary support for them without meddling in their plans  sakayanagi is surprised by the security  which  doesn t seem to fit this place  finds meeting the agenda free sakayanagi a  relief rather than a pain  notes he is  incorrigibly good  and could become an enemy if he learns the children s futures aren t guaranteed  guides him through the facility and seeks his assessment  values his support but distrusts his idealism","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Showing Sakayanagi the lab; the exam setup<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.101–103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Greets Sakayanagi at the guest room — he had been standing looking out the window rather than sitting on the sofa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-narimori.html\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry to keep you waiting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It can&#x27;t be helped. We can&#x27;t make this public right now. There are countless people desperately searching for scandals involving me and Naoe-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You were the one who helped with the White Room project the most. I wanted to show it to you first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No. For these three years, I&#x27;ve basically been hands-off. I&#x27;ve just continued to provide the necessary support for them without meddling in their plans.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Sakayanagi is surprised by the security, which &quot;doesn&#x27;t seem to fit this place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds meeting the agenda-free Sakayanagi a &quot;relief rather than a pain&quot;; notes he is &quot;incorrigibly good&quot; and could become an enemy if he learns the children&#x27;s futures aren&#x27;t guaranteed.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/b> Guides him through the facility and seeks his assessment; values his support but distrusts his idealism.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p96-1\">← Before: The drive to the facility; three years of the White Room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p104-1\">→ After: Watching the exam: the one-way mirror and the three groups<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p104-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"","w":"suzukake-tanji ishida-yuusuke souya ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi watching the exam  the one way mirror and the three groups stands with sakayanagi watching the children take a comprehensive exam through the glass that  became a one way mirror  the children each wear a researcher s nameplate and quietly take their seats  at  begin  all the children flip their papers over and take up pens  no one stands up  three year old motor development noted  standing on one foot  walking on tiptoes  smoothly climbing stairs  the test is math   addition  subtraction  multiplication  division  problems elementary students would tackle  suzukake s group doesn t move at all   the  first sense of discomfort  real time camera tracking shows some answer incorrectly but without panic  agitation or distress  suzukake plays flashy music  ishida s and souya s children stop and look around  but suzukake s students keep solving problems without excessive reaction  physical tests follow  ishida s children craft with small hands  souya s use horizontal bars and jungle gyms  suzukake s play the piano    far from professional  but more than adults could do with a little practice  watches suzukake s emotionless  fear trained children outperform the other two groups in both academics and physical skill  his brutal  education   punishment from newborns  fear until it  truly vanishes  eliminating emotions  wins  atsuomi puts him in charge of the second generation  his orthodox group shows natural human development but lesser results  his group shows natural development  horrified by suzukake s corporal punishment yet impressed by results","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Watching the exam: the one-way mirror and the three groups<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.104–108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands with Sakayanagi watching the children take a comprehensive exam through the glass that &quot;became a one-way mirror.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"suzukake-tanji.html\">Suzukake Tanji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishida-yuusuke\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#souya\">Sōya<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The children each wear a researcher&#x27;s nameplate and quietly take their seats.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> At &quot;Begin!&quot; all the children flip their papers over and take up pens; no one stands up.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Three-year-old motor development noted: standing on one foot, walking on tiptoes, smoothly climbing stairs.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The test is math — addition, subtraction, multiplication, division; problems elementary students would tackle.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Suzukake&#x27;s group doesn&#x27;t move at all — the &quot;first sense of discomfort&quot;; real-time camera tracking shows some answer incorrectly but without panic, agitation or distress.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Suzukake plays flashy music; Ishida&#x27;s and Souya&#x27;s children stop and look around, but Suzukake&#x27;s students keep solving problems without excessive reaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Physical tests follow: Ishida&#x27;s children craft with small hands; Souya&#x27;s use horizontal bars and jungle gyms; Suzukake&#x27;s play the piano — &quot;far from professional&quot; but more than adults could do with a little practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Watches Suzukake&#x27;s emotionless, fear-trained children outperform the other two groups in both academics and physical skill.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Suzukake Tanji<\/b> His brutal &quot;education&quot; (punishment from newborns, fear until it &quot;truly vanishes,&quot; eliminating emotions) wins; Atsuomi puts him in charge of the second generation.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/b> His orthodox group shows natural human development but lesser results.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sōya<\/b> His group shows natural development; horrified by Suzukake&#x27;s corporal punishment yet impressed by results.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p101-1\">← Before: Showing Sakayanagi the lab; the exam setup<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p109-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi&#x27;s objection; the decision to sacrifice himself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p109-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"spoken","w":"mika ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi sakayanagi s objection  the decision to sacrifice himself sakayanagi turns his back and leaves the lab  displeased with suzukake s methods   what s needed are exceptional abilities a brain that can surpass japan s top universities and win at the world s prestigious schools  physical abilities beyond olympic athletes  and an indomitable spirit that doesn t flinch even against world leaders   i understand what you re trying to say  your opinion will sufficiently act as a reference   without sacrificing yourself  there was no true success  realizes his words carry no weight because the education is someone else s   he must personally enter the white room as a subject to give the project persuasive power  pragmatic and relentless   dismisses sakayanagi s idealism as naive  and resolves to sacrifice himself to make the white room  change the world  calls her in the evening with a favor   the first step of his plan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi&#x27;s objection; the decision to sacrifice himself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.109–113<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakayanagi turns his back and leaves the lab, displeased with Suzukake&#x27;s methods.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"mika.html\">Mika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What&#x27;s needed are exceptional abilities—a brain that can surpass Japan&#x27;s top universities and win at the world&#x27;s prestigious schools, physical abilities beyond Olympic athletes, and an indomitable spirit that doesn&#x27;t flinch even…<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand what you&#x27;re trying to say. Your opinion will sufficiently act as a reference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Without sacrificing yourself, there was no true success.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What&#x27;s needed are exceptional abilities—a brain that can surpass Japan&#x27;s top universities and win at the world&#x27;s prestigious schools, physical abilities beyond Olympic athletes, and an indomitable spirit that doesn&#x27;t flinch even against world leaders.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes his words carry no weight because the education is someone else&#x27;s — he must personally enter the White Room as a subject to give the project persuasive power.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pragmatic and relentless — dismisses Sakayanagi&#x27;s idealism as naive, and resolves to sacrifice himself to make the White Room &quot;change the world.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.109–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mika<\/b> Calls her in the evening with a favor — the first step of his plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p104-1\">← Before: Watching the exam: the one-way mirror and the three groups<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p117-1\">→ After: Paying Mika; the naming of Kiyotaka<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p117-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"spoken","w":"mika ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi paying mika  the naming of kiyotaka meets mika in a room with bundles of bills arranged on a white table   fifty million yen in cash  no trace  the fifty million is the amount after deducting all childbirth and hospitalization expenses  mika is dressed in a suit she  probably wasn t used to wearing  a normal surrogacy would cost nearly half this at the high end   he pays more than double the market rate   money is heavy  but i can prepare as much as necessary to live  that s what the world s like on this side   i hardly remember ever doing so  well  maybe i ll pay them when i start a new job  so it s fine   no matter what  you will never be recognized as the mother in the future   that s none of your business  once the contract is finalized  our connection ends   you would do anything for money and yourself  that s the highest praise i can give you   names are just symbols  no matter who assigns them  a person s essence doesn t change   that suggestion is very like you  adds three million yen as a  celebration gift severance  hands her a pre filled divorce form  eleven days since the birth  three days left before registration  mika names the child  kiyotaka    after the host she is seeing  atsuomi writes  kiyotaka  in the register after she leaves  utterly cold and transactional   feels no attachment  offers his own child as a  cheap purchase  so long as he is useful for five years  and keeps mika as legal mother only to protect credibility  pays her for the surrogacy  severs all rights  and keeps her as a nominal wife  she names the child kiyotaka  his newborn son  named kiyotaka by mika  registered by atsuomi and destined to enter the white room as a fourth generation subject  waits in the next room  discusses disposing of mika","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Paying Mika; the naming of Kiyotaka<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.117–122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Mika in a room with bundles of bills arranged on a white table — fifty million yen in cash, no trace.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"mika.html\">Mika<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Money is heavy, but I can prepare as much as necessary to live. That&#x27;s what the world&#x27;s like on this side.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I hardly remember ever doing so. Well, maybe I&#x27;ll pay them when I start a new job, so it&#x27;s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No matter what, you will never be recognized as the mother in the future.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The fifty million is the amount after deducting all childbirth and hospitalization expenses; Mika is dressed in a suit she &quot;probably wasn&#x27;t used to wearing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> A normal surrogacy would cost nearly half this at the high end — he pays more than double the market rate.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s none of your business. Once the contract is finalized, our connection ends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You would do anything for money and yourself. That&#x27;s the highest praise I can give you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Names are just symbols. No matter who assigns them, a person&#x27;s essence doesn&#x27;t change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That suggestion is very like you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Adds three million yen as a &quot;celebration gift&quot;/severance; hands her a pre-filled divorce form; eleven days since the birth, three days left before registration.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Mika names the child &quot;Kiyotaka&quot; — after the host she is seeing. Atsuomi writes &quot;Kiyotaka&quot; in the register after she leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Utterly cold and transactional — feels no attachment, offers his own child as a &quot;cheap purchase&quot; so long as he is useful for five years, and keeps Mika as legal mother only to protect credibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mika<\/b> Pays her for the surrogacy, severs all rights, and keeps her as a nominal wife; she names the child Kiyotaka.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His newborn son, named Kiyotaka by Mika; registered by Atsuomi and destined to enter the White Room as a fourth-generation subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Waits in the next room; discusses disposing of Mika.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p109-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi&#x27;s objection; the decision to sacrifice himself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p124-1\">→ After: The Beta curriculum decision; 74 samples<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p124-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"spoken","w":"suzukake-tanji tabuchi ishida-yuusuke ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the beta curriculum decision  74 samples on the day kiyotaka arrives  gathers the researchers  tabuchi  with dark circles under his eyes  projects the curriculum onto a large screen  dropout rates  first generation 14  at age five  second 6  at age two  predicted  20  by five  third 6  at age one  predicted  25  ability increase between first and third generations  11 37  dropouts  problem  extremely low social adaptability   99  lived only in the white room  first generation knows the outside only through fragmented materials photos and can t imagine a cityscape  no real experience with vending machines  streetlights  shopping streets  convenience stores or supermarkets   adopt the beta curriculum   i said to adopt the beta curriculum  don t make me repeat myself   i will provide the strictest education to my own child  it s an excellent opportunity   frankly  i wouldn t mind if it kills them   i ve mostly picked up those who are disposable   we ll proceed as planned  send them to the facility we prepared and let them fend for themselves   just follow the orders  if you defy my commands  i won t hesitate to cut you off  even if it s you  kept the list of wealthy family children secret from researchers so they receive no special treatment  used the ooba group and dark brokers to acquire  disposable  samples  relentlessly experimental   applies the  unreachable  beta curriculum to his own son  assembles 74 samples  double the third generation  and crushes tabuchi s objections  orders him to adopt beta  suzukake regrets creating it but accepts  presents the data  resists and is told to obey or be cut off  objects  is it really  all right  atsuomi holds firm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Beta curriculum decision; 74 samples<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.124–129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the day Kiyotaka arrives, gathers the researchers; Tabuchi (with dark circles under his eyes) projects the curriculum onto a large screen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"suzukake-tanji.html\">Suzukake Tanji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#tabuchi\">Tabuchi<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishida-yuusuke\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Adopt the Beta curriculum.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I said to adopt the Beta curriculum. Don&#x27;t make me repeat myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I will provide the strictest education to my own child. It&#x27;s an excellent opportunity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Dropout rates: first generation 14% at age five; second 6% at age two (predicted &gt;20% by five); third 6% at age one (predicted &gt;25%). Ability increase between first and third generations: 11–37%.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Dropouts&#x27; problem: extremely low social adaptability — 99% lived only in the White Room; first generation knows the outside only through fragmented materials/photos and can&#x27;t imagine a cityscape; no real experience with vending machines, streetlights, shopping streets, convenience stores or supermarkets.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Frankly, I wouldn&#x27;t mind if it kills them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve mostly picked up those who are disposable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll proceed as planned. Send them to the facility we prepared and let them fend for themselves.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just follow the orders. If you defy my commands, I won&#x27;t hesitate to cut you off, even if it&#x27;s you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Kept the list of wealthy-family children secret from researchers so they receive no special treatment; used the Ooba group and dark brokers to acquire &quot;disposable&quot; samples.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Relentlessly experimental — applies the &quot;unreachable&quot; Beta curriculum to his own son, assembles 74 samples (double the third generation), and crushes Tabuchi&#x27;s objections.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Suzukake Tanji<\/b> Orders him to adopt Beta; Suzukake regrets creating it but accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tabuchi<\/b> Presents the data; resists and is told to obey or be cut off.<span class=\"pg\">p.124, 128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/b> Objects (&quot;Is it really… all right?&quot;); Atsuomi holds firm.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p117-1\">← Before: Paying Mika; the naming of Kiyotaka<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p129-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi&#x27;s phone call: offering to take his child<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p129-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-narimori ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi sakayanagi s phone call  offering to take his child steps into the corridor to answer a call from sakayanagi about the newborn   i ve been prepared ever since i decided to create this white room  a person in charge of educating abandoned babies can t expect to have a proper family   i see  i knew you would say that  dismisses sakayanagi s concern that his son deserves parental love  notes sakayanagi would raise his own unborn child with love and looks forward to it as one of his achievements  calls about the birth  offers to take atsuomi s child  intends to give his own unborn child all the love he can","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi&#x27;s phone call: offering to take his child<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.129–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Steps into the corridor to answer a call from Sakayanagi about the newborn.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-narimori.html\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve been prepared ever since I decided to create this White Room. A person in charge of educating abandoned babies can&#x27;t expect to have a proper family.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I see. I knew you would say that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dismisses Sakayanagi&#x27;s concern that his son deserves parental love; notes Sakayanagi would raise his own unborn child with love and looks forward to it as one of his achievements.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/b> Calls about the birth; offers to take Atsuomi&#x27;s child; intends to give his own unborn child all the love he can.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p124-1\">← Before: The Beta curriculum decision; 74 samples<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p199-1\">→ After: Naoe withdraws; the White Room scrapped<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p199-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi naoe withdraws  the white room scrapped at the ryoutei in sasagawa on a snowy january night  waits with kamogawa to report the white room s success to naoe sensei  tokyo is struck by unusually heavy snow  the garden visible from the corridor window is lit up  the meeting is over ten years after they first waited in the cold for naoe  kamogawa s father died of a myocardial infarction around this time last year  delivering the white room announcement had been kamogawa s goal   just achieve results that reach the heavens  don t be satisfied with just today  kamogawa   sorry to keep you waiting    naoe  arriving only  10 minutes late  i ve decided to withdraw my candidacy for the next party leader election   the calculations show that i m short by twenty to thirty votes   yet  kijima hasn t changed at all  he s taking politics seriously   for kijima  you ve become an eyesore   it s decided  it s a blank slate   if kijima acknowledges that you have no fangs  i ll put you forward again   don t joke with me  naoe withdraws because he is 20 30 votes short and the opposition plus kijima s clean record make running futile  he supports kijima to keep his position  and scraps the white room because atsuomi s flashy financial yakuza dealings have made him a liability  for the first time loses composure    don t joke with me    after over a decade of sacrificing everything for the project  resolves not to let it go to waste  his mentor and patron abandons him and the white room  atsuomi is ordered to  lay low  shares the shock  kamogawa s joy turns to despair at the  blank slate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Naoe withdraws; the White Room scrapped<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.199–207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the ryoutei in Sasagawa on a snowy January night, waits with Kamogawa to report the White Room&#x27;s success to Naoe-sensei.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Just achieve results that reach the heavens. Don&#x27;t be satisfied with just today, Kamogawa.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Sorry to keep you waiting.&quot; — Naoe, arriving only ~10 minutes late<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I&#x27;ve decided to withdraw my candidacy for the next party leader election.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Tokyo is struck by unusually heavy snow; the garden visible from the corridor window is lit up; the meeting is over ten years after they first waited in the cold for Naoe.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Kamogawa&#x27;s father died of a myocardial infarction around this time last year; delivering the White Room announcement had been Kamogawa&#x27;s goal.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;The calculations show that I&#x27;m short by twenty to thirty votes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Yet, Kijima hasn&#x27;t changed at all. He&#x27;s taking politics seriously.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;For Kijima, you&#x27;ve become an eyesore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s decided. It&#x27;s a blank slate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;If Kijima acknowledges that you have no fangs, I&#x27;ll put you forward again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;—Don&#x27;t joke with me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Naoe withdraws because he is 20–30 votes short and the opposition plus Kijima&#x27;s clean record make running futile; he supports Kijima to keep his position, and scraps the White Room because Atsuomi&#x27;s flashy financial/yakuza dealings have made him a liability.<span class=\"pg\">p.202–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> For the first time loses composure — &quot;Don&#x27;t joke with me&quot; — after over a decade of sacrificing everything for the project; resolves not to let it go to waste.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> His mentor and patron abandons him and the White Room; Atsuomi is ordered to &quot;lay low.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Shares the shock; Kamogawa&#x27;s joy turns to despair at the &quot;blank slate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199–207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p129-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi&#x27;s phone call: offering to take his child<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p219-1\">→ After: The funding party: President Amasawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p219-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"amasawa-president amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the funding party  president amasawa at a party  negotiates with president amasawa  who wants his unborn child placed in the white room   we re already taking care of your daughter in the white room  president amasawa   this year  i ll double last year s amount  i ll give one hundred million    amasawa  unless there s a special reason  visits are basically impossible  you can only meet your children regularly after they become adults or leave the white room   as for the future  please do as you like  ayanokouji sensei  after all  that was a test tube baby  and i don t really feel like she s my own child    amasawa amasawa s wife wants to give birth in japan  she is a  hawaii enthusiast  and suspects cheating  he treats the white room as convenient daycare  offers  100 million  never visits his daughter  and hums happily  maintains control of tone with a billionaire  ensuring he isn t offended  sees such children as profitable  no danger additions  negotiates financing  the president entrusts another child to the white room  amasawa s test tube daughter  the second most developed fifth generation student","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p219-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The funding party: President Amasawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.219–223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At a party, negotiates with President Amasawa, who wants his unborn child placed in the White Room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#amasawa-president\">Amasawa (President)<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;We&#x27;re already taking care of your daughter in the White Room, President Amasawa.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;This year, I&#x27;ll double last year&#x27;s amount. I&#x27;ll give one hundred million.&quot; — Amasawa<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Unless there&#x27;s a special reason, visits are basically impossible. You can only meet your children regularly after they become adults or leave the White Room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;As for the future, please do as you like, Ayanokouji-sensei. After all, that was a test-tube baby, and I don&#x27;t really feel like she&#x27;s my own child.&quot; — Amasawa<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Amasawa&#x27;s wife wants to give birth in Japan (she is a &quot;Hawaii enthusiast&quot;) and suspects cheating; he treats the White Room as convenient daycare, offers ¥100 million, never visits his daughter, and hums happily.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Maintains control of tone with a billionaire, ensuring he isn&#x27;t offended; sees such children as profitable, no-danger additions.<span class=\"pg\">p.219–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa (President)<\/b> Negotiates financing; the president entrusts another child to the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.219–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Amasawa&#x27;s test-tube daughter, the second most developed fifth-generation student.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p199-1\">← Before: Naoe withdraws; the White Room scrapped<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p232-1\">→ After: The children&#x27;s dispute; Kanzaki and Ishigami; Sakayanagi&#x27;s farewell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p232-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ishigami-kyou kanzaki-ryuuji sakayanagi-narimori nogi fuji ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the children s dispute  kanzaki and ishigami  sakayanagi s farewell watches a group of party children bullying one boy  fuji  over a kazuya autograph  five boys  three surround fuji  nogi the leader  ryuuji and ishigami also present  the leader demands a vote  ishigami defends fuji  reasons the claim of being the first to receive an autograph can t be proven  and tricks nogi into grabbing his collar before calling for help from adults   atsuomi notes ishigami deliberately didn t choose him because atsuomi had only observed   i noticed early on that fuji was calling for help  yet you just stood by and observed  i couldn t be sure you d be on our side    ishigami  if you don t have the power to help  you might as well just give up and run away  but if you do have the power and don t use it  then you re a fool   being associated with a man like me would pose many problems for you as the chairman of anhs   i have to solidify the white room and send personnel capable of overhauling the country s organizational structure  then  i plan to overturn that system from the ground up   good luck  sakayanagi  let s meet again someday  reads people sharply  gives ryuuji a calculated  lecture  in front of his father to keep kanzaki engineering s investment  and lays out a 10 20 year plan to overturn japan s seniority bound political system from within  the clever son of the ishigami group president  atsuomi is impressed by his calm and is asked  noncommittally  to take him into politics later  ryuuji  son of kanzaki tomohiro  atsuomi lectures him about using one s power to help others  becomes anhs chairman and must distance himself from atsuomi  they part on good terms  nogi pharmaceuticals  son  the bullying leader  the boy falsely accused of lying about the autograph","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p232-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The children&#x27;s dispute; Kanzaki and Ishigami; Sakayanagi&#x27;s farewell<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.232–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches a group of party children bullying one boy (Fuji) over a Kazuya autograph.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-narimori.html\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#nogi\">Nogi<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#fuji\">Fuji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I noticed early on that Fuji was calling for help, yet you just stood by and observed. I couldn&#x27;t be sure you&#x27;d be on our side.&quot; — Ishigami<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;If you don&#x27;t have the power to help, you might as well just give up and run away. But if you do have the power and don&#x27;t use it, then you&#x27;re a fool.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Being associated with a man like me would pose many problems for you as the chairman of ANHS.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Five boys; three surround Fuji, Nogi the leader, Ryuuji and Ishigami also present; the leader demands a vote; Ishigami defends Fuji, reasons the claim of being the first to receive an autograph can&#x27;t be proven, and tricks Nogi into grabbing his collar before calling for help from adults — Atsuomi notes Ishigami deliberately didn&#x27;t choose him because Atsuomi had only observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.224–230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I have to solidify the White Room and send personnel capable of overhauling the country&#x27;s organizational structure. Then, I plan to overturn that system from the ground up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Good luck, Sakayanagi. Let&#x27;s meet again someday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads people sharply, gives Ryuuji a calculated &quot;lecture&quot; in front of his father to keep Kanzaki Engineering&#x27;s investment, and lays out a 10–20 year plan to overturn Japan&#x27;s seniority-bound political system from within.<span class=\"pg\">p.232–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> The clever son of the Ishigami Group president; Atsuomi is impressed by his calm and is asked (noncommittally) to take him into politics later.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Ryuuji, son of Kanzaki Tomohiro; Atsuomi lectures him about using one&#x27;s power to help others.<span class=\"pg\">p.234–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/b> Becomes ANHS chairman and must distance himself from Atsuomi; they part on good terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nogi<\/b> Nogi Pharmaceuticals&#x27; son, the bullying leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fuji<\/b> The boy falsely accused of lying about the autograph.<span class=\"pg\">p.224–230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p219-1\">← Before: The funding party: President Amasawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p247-1\">→ After: Returning to Tokyo; preparing the comeback<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p247-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"naoe-sensei kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi returning to tokyo  preparing the comeback returns to tokyo from saitama as cherry blossoms bloom  goes to his long unused office instead of his meguro home   you ve grown old  naoe  naoe  the fixer in kijima s shadow  is over eighty and was seriously ill   officially recovered but in reality his life hangs by a thread  his sabotage of the white room is proof he means to eliminate atsuomi before he dies   it s frustrating that i can t bury him with my own hands  but having him buried by illness might be best    kamogawa  that s why we need to make sure the timing is right when we go for the kill  sees the white room s freeze as a setback but readies a counterattack  notes kijima  in his sixties  could stay in power another ten or twenty years  making this  the last chance to strike  his old mentor is now an enemy dying by inches  atsuomi waits for his health to fail  meets him by the office  they discuss timing and naoe s deteriorating health","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p247-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Returning to Tokyo; preparing the comeback<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.247–250<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to Tokyo from Saitama as cherry blossoms bloom; goes to his long-unused office instead of his Meguro home.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;You&#x27;ve grown old, Naoe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It&#x27;s frustrating that I can&#x27;t bury him with my own hands, but having him buried by illness might be best.&quot; — Kamogawa<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;That&#x27;s why we need to make sure the timing is right when we go for the kill.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Naoe, the fixer in Kijima&#x27;s shadow, is over eighty and was seriously ill — officially recovered but in reality his life hangs by a thread; his sabotage of the White Room is proof he means to eliminate Atsuomi before he dies.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees the White Room&#x27;s freeze as a setback but readies a counterattack; notes Kijima (in his sixties) could stay in power another ten or twenty years, making this &quot;the last chance to strike.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">naoe-sensei<\/b> His old mentor is now an enemy dying by inches; Atsuomi waits for his health to fail.<span class=\"pg\">p.247–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Meets him by the office; they discuss timing and Naoe&#x27;s deteriorating health.<span class=\"pg\">p.247–249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p232-1\">← Before: The children&#x27;s dispute; Kanzaki and Ishigami; Sakayanagi&#x27;s farewell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p249-1\">→ After: Moving the children; the plan for Kiyotaka<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p249-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi moving the children  the plan for kiyotaka arranges the children s temporary supervision at a purchased orphanage and waits for kiyotaka to be brought from a counseling clinic   as planned  the children are temporarily being supervised and managed at the orphanage we purchased    tabuchi  i have no intention of favoring him just because he s my son   he s a monster  you shouldn t look at him with such a frivolous attitude    ishida kiyotaka was sent to the clinic because a major funder s daughter desperately wanted to meet him   atsuomi calls it a  shallow idea  that heals wounds in a counterproductive way  ishida calls kiyotaka a  monster  having watched him since birth  deliberately avoids favoritism toward his son in public  yet calls him the white room s  greatest masterpiece  with the  qualifications","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p249-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Moving the children; the plan for Kiyotaka<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.249–256<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arranges the children&#x27;s temporary supervision at a purchased orphanage and waits for Kiyotaka to be brought from a counseling clinic.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;As planned, the children are temporarily being supervised and managed at the orphanage we purchased.&quot; — Tabuchi<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I have no intention of favoring him just because he&#x27;s my son.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;He&#x27;s a monster. You shouldn&#x27;t look at him with such a frivolous attitude.&quot; — Ishida<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Kiyotaka was sent to the clinic because a major funder&#x27;s daughter desperately wanted to meet him — Atsuomi calls it a &quot;shallow idea&quot; that heals wounds in a counterproductive way; Ishida calls Kiyotaka a &quot;monster,&quot; having watched him since birth.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately avoids favoritism toward his son in public, yet calls him the White Room&#x27;s &quot;greatest masterpiece&quot; with the &quot;qualifications.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p247-1\">← Before: Returning to Tokyo; preparing the comeback<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p259-1\">→ After: The political plan; Tsukishiro enlisted<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p259-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"tsukishiro kamogawa ayanokouji-atsuomi","q":"ayanokoji atsuomi the political plan  tsukishiro enlisted left alone with kamogawa after dropping kiyotaka off  lays out his political ambitions   it s the fact that the ultimate  perfected existence only exists in one person   it s frustrating that there s an age limit in the political world  it s the first time i ve felt this way   the earliest kiyotaka can become an elected official  after reaching adulthood  is at age twenty five  by then  i ll be sixty one   i haven t decided yet   if either i or kiyotaka can dominate the political scene  we could significantly change japan without having to discuss matters fifty or a hundred years into the future  weighing whether to make kiyotaka a politician   the  ultimate  perfected existence  exists in only one person  notes the disadvantage of nepotism and his son s lack of emotions and worldly knowledge  and begins preparing to change the plan and develop kiyotaka s individuality  enlisted to handle background arrangements  agrees to cooperate when atsuomi implements his plan  left in shock by the plan  kept close","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p259-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The political plan; Tsukishiro enlisted<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.259–260<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Left alone with Kamogawa after dropping Kiyotaka off, lays out his political ambitions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It&#x27;s the fact that the ultimate, perfected existence only exists in one person.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It&#x27;s frustrating that there&#x27;s an age limit in the political world; it&#x27;s the first time I&#x27;ve felt this way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;The earliest Kiyotaka can become an elected official, after reaching adulthood, is at age twenty-five. By then, I&#x27;ll be sixty-one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I haven&#x27;t decided yet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;If either I or Kiyotaka can dominate the political scene, we could significantly change Japan without having to discuss matters fifty or a hundred years into the future.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighing whether to make Kiyotaka a politician — the &quot;ultimate, perfected existence&quot; exists in only one person; notes the disadvantage of nepotism and his son&#x27;s lack of emotions and worldly knowledge, and begins preparing to change the plan and develop Kiyotaka&#x27;s individuality.<span class=\"pg\">p.259–260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Enlisted to handle background arrangements; agrees to cooperate when Atsuomi implements his plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.260–261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Left in shock by the plan; kept close.<span class=\"pg\">p.259–260<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-atsuomi-y0-p249-1\">← Before: Moving the children; the plan for Kiyotaka<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
